		bodyHtml: `<p>The chapter begins with a loss: &ldquo;After Moses our Father's servant died, our Father told Joshua son of Nun, Moses' assistant:&rdquo; (Joshua 1:1). Joshua had served beside Moses for years. Now he is the one who must lead, and our Father speaks to him directly.</p><p>The first command is to move: &ldquo;Moses my servant is dead. Now get up, cross the Jordan, you and all these people, into the land I am giving them, the children of Israel.&rdquo; (Joshua 1:2). Verse 9 is the end of that speech, not a stand-alone slogan. It is spoken to one man at a doorway, with an army and a river in front of him.`,
