		heading: `The promise under the command`,
		bodyHtml: `<p>Before our Father says &ldquo;be strong&rdquo; the first time, he gives the reason: &ldquo;No one will stand against you all your life. As I was with Moses, I will be with you; I will not leave or abandon you.&rdquo; (Joshua 1:5). The courage he asks for is built on a promise he has already made.</p><p>The same pattern closes the speech. &ldquo;Have I not commanded you? Be strong and courageous. Do not fear or be discouraged, for I, your Father, am with you wherever you go.&rdquo; (Joshua 1:9). The command comes with its reason attached: <em>for I, your Father, am with you</em>. Courage here is not a mood to work up. It is the right response to knowing who is beside you.`,
