	{
		id: "repeated",
		heading: `Why he says it three times`,
		bodyHtml: `<p>The call is repeated: &ldquo;Be strong and courageous, for you will lead these people to inherit the land I swore to their ancestors I would give them.&rdquo; (Joshua 1:6). Then again: &ldquo;Only be strong and very courageous, careful to obey all the law Moses my servant commanded you.&rdquo; (Joshua 1:7). Then a third time in verse 9.</p><p>Each time, something different is tied to it. In verse 6 the ground is the promise to the ancestors. In verse 7 it is faithfulness to what our Father has already said. In verse 9 it is his presence. Joshua is not told to feel brave. He is told what to stand on.`,
